Login page: the brand is the image logo, not the router's name

Footstrap prints the router's hostname where a login page usually carries its
maker: `<p class="fs-login-host">` holds `boardinfo.hostname`, so a CleanWRT
router shows the word "CleanWRT" - and shows whatever else an admin named the
device, which is not a brand. This replaces that one line with the CleanWRT logo
as an image, named in its `alt` text so the accessible name stays what the
comment above the line asks for. The file it points at is not part of the theme:
it is this repository's own overlay at `files/www/luci-static/cw-branding/login-logo.png`,
outside the theme's directory, so a theme update cannot overwrite it and this
patch cannot collide with it. The page's own heading (`Authorization Required`)
is already clipped for sighted users and stays the single heading.

Applies to: https://github.com/VizzleTF/luci-theme-footstrap.git
            @ a1711eda02fefe87a12590bae9eaa80c373a4bd9 (pinned in configs/local-packages.pin)
Applied by: tools/cw-release-build.sh, on the pinned commit before the package is
            installed, with `patch -p1 --fuzz=0` - the build fails if upstream
            changes this line; re-port it then.
Upstream status: not submitted (CleanWRT-specific branding).

--- a/luci-theme-footstrap/ucode/template/themes/footstrap/sysauth.ut
+++ b/luci-theme-footstrap/ucode/template/themes/footstrap/sysauth.ut
@@ -38,7 +38,7 @@
 	 `Authorization Required` below stays the one heading (clipped by .fs-sr), or a screen reader
 	 hears the hostname as a section title.
 	-#}
-	<p class="fs-login-host">{{ entityencode(striptags(boardinfo.hostname ?? 'OpenWrt'), true) }}</p>
+	<p class="fs-login-host"><img src="/luci-static/cw-branding/login-logo.png" alt="CleanWRT" width="260" height="192" /></p>
 	{#
 	 Two independent alerts: neither variable alone says which dispatcher branch rendered this.
 	 `fuser` is set in both branches, including the OTP step after a correct password; and
